1. Launch ec2 => google it
2. create a volume with 10G size, GP3 => google it 
3. attach the volume to to instance, dev name /dev/sdb => google it
switch to root => sudo -i 
4. exporle current disk
   a. lsblk => see disk name, size, mountpoint
   b. df -h => see current disk usage
5. mkfs.xfs <devicename> => create file system in the volume
6. edit /etc/fstab => to mount this disk to /videos 
   a. note you need to create /videos 
7. mount -a => to mount the volumes in /etc/fstab
8. reboot and make sure that the mount persist 



